.TH QRGEN 3 "2026" "y-- standard library" "y-- Library Reference"
.SH NAME
QRgen \- QR code generation
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B QRgen
module generates QR codes from text strings.
On import, the following global constants are set:
.B ECC_LEVEL_LOW, ECC_LEVEL_MEDIUM, ECC_LEVEL_QUARTILE, ECC_LEVEL_HIGH.
.PP
.B NOTE:
Due to a suspected bug in the source (line 20802: env->set("Math", ...)),
the module may be accessible under the name "Math" at the language level
rather than "QRgen".
.B NEEDS VERIFICATION.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.SS GenerateQRcode
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
QRcodeObj() GenerateQRcode(text: string(), eccLevel: int())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Generates a QR code for
.I text
at error-correction level
.IR eccLevel .
Returns a QRcodeObj instance with fields:
.RS
.TP
Version (int())
QR version (1-40).
.TP
Size (int())
Modules per side.
.TP
BoolArray (tuple())
Size x Size tuple of tuples of bool(); BoolArray[x][y] is true for a dark module.
.TP
CorrectionLevel (int())
ECC level used.
.RE
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR (not 2 args); C++ exceptions for unencodable input (NEEDS VERIFICATION).
.TP
\fBEXAMPLES\fR
.EX
qr = GenerateQRcode("hello", ECC_LEVEL_LOW)
qr.Size  -> 21
.EE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
Json(3)
